From 16c335d0aacdcaf9c7ffc0fe0eac6eba00a2a121 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 21:09:20 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] NOOVERLAP-B (web): Contact Force page overlaps removed (Load
 rate groups drawn like golden run time)

EastSun 20260930: overlapping controls are not allowed.
Scanner (offline, 9 tab states): 43 defects -> 0 at 100%.
- The four Load rate tabs use a page-local maker makeContactForceGroupRT
  that follows golden's RUN-TIME layout: ContactForce.cpp:21-206
  THTSLKClass, :209-328 THTDieForceOneByOneSLKClass, :331 THTDieForce-
  SLKClass, :1439 THTSLKIndClass constructors + FormShow :822-865 (not an
  NS kit -> the NS row is hidden; heater offset only with CosFunction.
  bUseLoadCellOffsetByHeater, not set for CC_PTI); each group 100 high,
  alTop-stacked, caption inside the box. The shared hwidgets.js
  makeContactForceGroup drew the dfm's Visible=False design-time
  template (both rows, other field positions, caption outside the box)
  and is left untouched; this page no longer calls it. Display only:
  these groups carry no data or commands (as before).
- Web-font fixes inside the new maker: offset label 14px (16px text is
  wider than MS Sans Serif and hit the field), TrackBar 272px with
  margin 0 (golden 275 covers the Load rate field by 3px).
- New Method tab: the eight lab*Num values 5px right (golden Left=736,
  the TrackBar ends at 60+677=737).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
